# Grid: across pages, Split rows: true breaks a row that does not fit and false moves it whole to the next page.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Grid · Split rows
	Page:
		Paper: A6
		Margin: 12mm
	Styles:
		For style: cell
			Box:
				Padding: 6
				Background: sand
			Typography:
				Size: 8
				Line height: 11
	Section:
		Text: Grid
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Split rows
		Paragraph: A `Grid` breaks between rows. A row taller than what is left of the page is broken there, its items in parallel, with `Split rows: true` (the default). With `false` it moves whole to the next page.
			Style: intro
		Text: Split rows: false
			Style: label
		Grid:
			Column sizes: * *
			Gap: 8
			Split rows: false
			Area:
				Text: Row 1
					Style: cell
			Area:
				Text: Row 1
					Style: cell
			Area:
				Text:
					Style: cell
					Content >>
						Row 2 does not fit under row 1, so it moves whole to the next page and leaves the rest of this page empty.
						A row is only broken with false when it does not fit on a whole page either.
						The engine looks for the place of the break between rows first.
						This row is taller than what is left of the first page.
						Its two items move together.
						It suits rows that are read as one piece, such as the entries of a timetable or the cards of a catalog.
						The label above the grid stays on the first page, with the first row.
			Area:
				Text: Row 2
					Style: cell
		Text: Split rows: true
			Style: label
		Grid:
			Column sizes: * *
			Gap: 8
			Area:
				Text: Row 1
					Style: cell
			Area:
				Text: Row 1
					Style: cell
			Area:
				Text:
					Style: cell
					Content >>
						Row 2 starts on this page and goes on at the top of the next one, because the row is split where the page ends.
						Each item of the row is broken between its own lines.
						Widows and orphans still apply to the text of each item.
						The background of the item is broken with it.
						The second part of the row goes on the next page.
						There, the row ends after these lines.
			Area:
				Text:
					Style: cell
					Content >>
						The other item of row 2 is broken at the same height.
						Its last lines go on the next page.
